# Verify actual current state before acting

Before taking any consequential action — applying a fix, assuming a process completed, or relying on a prior assumption — always verify the actual current state of the system. Do not assume that expected conditions still hold, that a prior step succeeded silently, or that historical context (aged todos, prior runs) reflects today's reality.

## Procedures
- Before applying a fix from any issue or todo, read the current code/state to confirm the root cause still exists and has not already been addressed.
- After running any batch operation, explicitly enumerate the intended targets and confirm each one was processed — do not rely solely on a clean exit code.
- When presented with a claim about system state, ground it in a direct observation (file read, log line, test output) before acting on it.

